<title>GREECE: Greece to issue T-bills at lower rates on Oct 31.</title>
<headline>Greece to issue T-bills at lower rates on Oct 31.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece will issue three-, six- and 12-month T-bills at 11.50 percent, 11.70 percent and 12.30 percent respectively on October 31, down by 40 basis points on its end-September issue, the finance ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>The T-bills will be available for one day on book-entry and physical forms, it said. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
